<title>GERMANY: Pan-German Oct industry output falls 1.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Pan-German Oct industry output falls 1.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The economics ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT  Oct 96    Sept 96	Oct 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)   -1.8	 -0.6	 -1.9</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     -0.2	 -0.3	 -2.3</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		96.9	 98.7	 97.1</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional. The year-on-year figures are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank statistics.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				    Oct 96		  Sept 96</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Mining			74.9	+1.2	74.0	 +0.7</p>
<p> Manufacturing output    95.3	-2.0	97.2	-0.5</p>
<p> Incl:Intermed. goods    99.1	-1.9     101.0	-0.6</p>
<p>	Capital goods	94.7	-2.1	96.7	+1.4</p>
<p>	Consumer durables  82.6	-2.5	84.7	-7.6</p>
<p>	Consumer goods     94.3	-1.5	95.7	-0.9</p>
<p> Energy output	    102.0	-0.5     102.5	-3.5</p>
<p> Construction	     113.7	-1.8     115.8	+0.1</p>
<p>Two month comparison Sept/Oct 96 with July/Aug 96:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     -1.5</p>
<p> Manufacturing output		  -1.5</p>
<p> Construction			    -2.5</p>
<p> Capital goods			   unch</p>
<p> Mining				    +0.5</p>
<p> Energy output			   -3.5</p>
<p> Consumer durables		     -7.0</p>
<p> Consumer goods			  -1.5</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    -1.0</p>
<p>Two month comparison Sept/Oct 1996 with Sept/Oct 1995:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     +0.2</p>
<p> Mining				    -5.5</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		 +1.2</p>
<p>  Incl: Intermediate goods	   -0.1</p>
<p>	  Capital goods		  +3.5</p>
<p>	  Consumer durables	    +2.4</p>
<p>	  Consumer goods		 -0.5</p>
<p> Energy output			   +2.3</p>
<p> Construction			    -5.8</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
